        "title": "Pericallis",
        "language": "en",
        "scope": "verified_requested_taxon",
        "passages": [
          {
            "id": "s1:p1",
            "text": "Pericallis is a small genus of 15 species of flowering plants in the family Asteraceae, native to the Canary Islands, Madeira and Azores. The genus includes herbaceous plants and small subshrubs. In the past, the genus was often included in either Cineraria or Senecio."
          },
          {
            "id": "s1:p2",
            "text": "The florist's cineraria (Pericallis × hybrida) is a hybrid between P. cruenta and P. lanata."
          },
          {
            "id": "s1:p3",
            "text": "Species\nSpecies include:\nPericallis appendiculata (L.f.) B.Nord.\nPericallis aurita (L'Hér.) B.Nord.\nPericallis cruenta (L'Hér.) Bolle\nPericallis echinata (L.f.) B.Nord.\nPericallis hadrosoma (Svent.) B.Nord.\nPericallis hansenii (G.Kunkel) Sunding\nPericallis lanata (L'Hér.) B.Nord.\nPericallis malvifolia (L'Hér.) B.Nord.\nPericallis menezesii R. Jardim, K. E. Jones, Carine & M. Seq.\nPericallis multiflora (L'Hér.) B.Nord.\nPericallis murrayi (Bornm.) B.Nord.\nPericallis papyracea (DC.) B.Nord.\nPericallis steetzii (Bolle) B.Nord.\nPericallis tussilaginis (L'Hér.) D.Don\nPericallis webbii (Sch. Bip.) Bolle"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "s2",
